	"tutorialDesc": "The starting valleys of Chronos Settlement drawn by hand (sim/startValleys.ts), laid over the generated land round a new town’s camp. Paint the Ground (an empty cell keeps the land’s own, so fray the edges into it), the Relief where the lie of the land isn’t level (a range needs mountain ground; high ground is climbed by a ramp), put one Camp where the town’s fire goes (keep its meadow open: five cells round it), and Landmarks to be drawn on the cells. Water that runs off the valley’s edge runs on to the land’s. After editing, run `node tools/ldtk-maps.mjs` to make src/shared/data/startValleys.ts.",
	"customCommands": [],
	"flags": [
		"UseMultilinesType"
	],
